{"id":20817,"path":"/grammar-points/b2/possessive-s-with-time-expressions-two-hours-walk/","parentId":534,"order":270,"section":"grammar-points","level":"b2","depth":3,"title":"Possessive ’s with time expressions: Two hours’ walk","seo":{"title":"Possessive ’s with time expressions: Two hours’ walk - Test-English","description":"Possessive ’s with time expressions - Two hours’ walk. Learn how to use the possessive 's with time expressions with a detailed explanation and three exercises","image":"/media/uploads/possessive-s-with-time-expressions.jpg"},"modified":"2025-05-13T10:00:29","kind":"lesson","parts":["<h3>Exercise 1</h3> <h5>Choose the correct option to complete the sentences below.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"751\"></div>","<h3>Exercise 2</h3> <h5>Rewrite these phrases using <em>‘s</em> or <em>‘</em> (apostrophe).</h5> <p><em>EXAMPLE: a two-hour hike ⇒ <span class=\"textGap\">two hours’ hike</span></em><br> </p><div data-quiz=\"752\"></div> <p></p>"],"explanation":"<h2>The use of the possessive ‘<strong>s</strong> with time expressions</h2> <p>We don’t normally use the <a href=\"/grammar-points/b2/compound-nouns-possessive-forms/\">possessive<strong> ‘s</strong></a> with inanimate things. In those cases, we generally use <strong>of</strong> instead. For example, we say:</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>the end <span><strong>of</strong></span> the street</em> <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></li> <li><em>the <span><strong>street’s end <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></strong></span></em></li> <li><em>the first page <span><strong>of</strong></span> the document&nbsp;</em><img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></li> <li><em>the <span><strong>document’s first page <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></strong></span></em></li> </ul> <p>However, the possessive <strong>‘s</strong> is often used in time expressions to talk about the duration of something. For example:</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>You need <span><strong>two years’ experience</strong></span> to get a job.</em></li> <li><em>He lives <span><strong>one hour’s drive</strong></span> from the airport.</em></li> <li><em>The<span><strong> three hours’ journey</strong></span> to the valley was amazing.</em></li> </ul> <p>🔍 <strong>Note</strong> that the apostrophe is sometimes not included, but this is usually not considered correct.</p> <h2>When do we need to use the possessive <strong>‘s</strong> with time expressions?</h2> <p><img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-31527\" src=\"/media/uploads/Possessive-s-with-time-expressions_B2-grammar-chart.webp\" alt=\"A grammar chart explaining the use of the possessive 's with time words, showing examples like &quot;three hours' journey,&quot; &quot;one hour's drive,&quot; and &quot;two years' experience,&quot; alongside their equivalent forms using &quot;of.&quot;\" width=\"500\" height=\"500\" loading=\"lazy\"></p> <h6></h6> <p>If you are not sure whether you should use the possessive <strong>‘s</strong> with a time expression, you can try replacing it with the word <strong>of</strong>. If the expression still makes sense, it means that you should use the <strong>‘</strong> (apostrophe) or <strong>‘s</strong>.<br> <br> For example, we say:</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>two years<span><strong>‘</strong></span> experience (=an experience <span><strong>of</strong></span> two years)</em></li> <li><em>one hour<span><strong>‘</strong></span><span><strong>s</strong></span> drive (=a drive <span><strong>of</strong></span> one hour)</em></li> <li><em>three hours<strong><span>‘ </span></strong> journey (=a journey <span><strong>of</strong></span> three hours)</em></li> </ul> <p>But we say:</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>It’s two months old.</em> (‘<em>two months of old’</em> does not make sense.)</li> <li><em>She is nine months pregnant.</em> (‘<em>nine months of pregnant’ d</em>oes not make sense.)</li> </ul> <h2>The possessive <strong>‘s</strong> with singular and plural time expressions</h2> <p>The <a href=\"/grammar-points/b2/compound-nouns-possessive-forms/\">form of the possessive <strong>‘s</strong></a> with time expressions is the same as with other nouns.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li>Add <strong>‘s</strong> after singular nouns: <em>one year<span><strong>‘s</strong></span> notice, an hour<span><strong>‘</strong><strong>s</strong></span> walk, etc.</em></li> <li>Add only <strong>‘</strong> (apostrophe) after plural nouns ending in <strong>-s</strong>: three years<span><strong>‘</strong></span> notice, two hours<span><strong>‘</strong></span> walk, etc.</li> </ul> <h2>A two-day journey = two days’ journey</h2> <p><img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21512\" src=\"/media/uploads/Compound-adjectives-with-number.png\" alt=\"Compound adjectives with numbers\" width=\"500\" height=\"501\" loading=\"lazy\"></p> <h6></h6> <p>We also often use <strong>number + time expression</strong> before nouns to talk about how long something lasts.&nbsp; In this case, the number and the time expression are joined by a hyphen, and the time word is singular.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>a <span><strong>four-hour </strong><span>journey</span></span> = four hours’ journey</em></li> <li><em>a <strong><span>thirty-minute </span></strong><span>delay</span> = thirty minutes’ delay</em></li> <li><em>a <strong><span>two-hour </span></strong><span><span>drive</span></span> = two hours’ drive</em></li> </ul> <p>🔍 <strong>Note</strong> that this type of <strong>number + noun</strong> compound adjective is also used to talk about other kinds of measurements.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>a <span><strong>one-hundred-dollar</strong></span> bill</em></li> <li><em>a <span><strong>five-litre</strong></span> bottle</em></li> <li><em>a <strong><span>twenty-foot</span></strong> container</em></li> </ul>","quizzes":[{"id":751,"questions":[{"id":6387,"num":"1","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>The campsite is just _____ bike ride from the beach. </div>","choices":[{"id":11047,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>a ten-minutes </span>"},{"id":11048,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>ten minutes'</span>"},{"id":11049,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>ten minute</span>"}]},{"id":6397,"num":"2","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>You can get _____ massage for free!</div>","choices":[{"id":11077,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>a 30-minute</span>"},{"id":11078,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>a 30-minutes</span>"},{"id":11079,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>30 minute's</span>"}]},{"id":6389,"num":"3","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>You owe me _____ rent.</div>","choices":[{"id":11053,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>two months'</span>"},{"id":11054,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>two months</span>"},{"id":11055,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>two month's</span>"}]},{"id":6390,"num":"4","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>I will have _____ vacation at Christmas.</div>","choices":[{"id":11056,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>five days' </span>"},{"id":11057,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>five day's</span>"},{"id":11058,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>five-days</span>"}]},{"id":6396,"num":"5","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>After only _____ journey, we were exhausted.</div>","choices":[{"id":11074,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>a days'</span>"},{"id":11075,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>two days's</span>"},{"id":11076,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>a day's</span>"}]},{"id":6394,"num":"6","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>_____ delay is not really a delay.</div>","choices":[{"id":11068,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>Five minutes' </span>"},{"id":11069,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>Five minutes</span>"},{"id":11070,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>A five-minutes</span>"}]},{"id":6395,"num":"7","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>You should give your employer _____ notice before leaving your job.</div>","choices":[{"id":11071,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>two week</span>"},{"id":11072,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>two week's</span>"},{"id":11073,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>two weeks'</span>"}]},{"id":6398,"num":"8","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>_____ walk per day is an excellent way to stay fit and healthy.</div>","choices":[{"id":11080,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>A 40-minutes</span>"},{"id":11081,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>40 minute's</span>"},{"id":11082,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>A 40-minute</span>"}]},{"id":6410,"num":"9","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>You all deserve _____ coffee break.</div>","choices":[{"id":11083,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>a ten-minutes</span>"},{"id":11084,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>ten minute's</span>"},{"id":11085,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>ten minutes'</span>"}]},{"id":6411,"num":"10","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>They started their business after _____ planning.</div>","choices":[{"id":11086,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>two year</span>"},{"id":11087,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>two years'</span>"},{"id":11088,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>two year's</span>"}]}]},{"id":752,"questions":[{"id":6399,"num":"1","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>a five-hour drive ⇒ <span data-gap=\"0\"></span></p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":6400,"num":"2","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>six months of insurance ⇒ <span data-gap=\"0\"></span></p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":6403,"num":"3","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>a one-week suspension ⇒ <span data-gap=\"0\"></span></p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":6401,"num":"4","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>a two-week investigation ⇒ <span data-gap=\"0\"></span></p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":6402,"num":"5","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>a time of four years ⇒ <span data-gap=\"0\"></span></p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":6404,"num":"6","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>one day of work ⇒ <span data-gap=\"0\"></span></p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":6405,"num":"7","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>eight hours of sleep ⇒ <span data-gap=\"0\"></span></p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":6406,"num":"8","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>a two-week holiday ⇒ <span data-gap=\"0\"></span></p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":6408,"num":"9","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>two weeks of salary ⇒ <span data-gap=\"0\"></span></p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":6409,"num":"10","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>a three-day trip ⇒ <span data-gap=\"0\"></span></p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]}]}]}